  "source": "Cantilever columns (Euler-Bernoulli, no beams, joints free to rotate) joined at each level only by the rigid diaphragm: lateral flexibility a^2 (3b - a) / 6EI between heights a <= b, torsion GJ/h per story; UX, UY, RZ of both levels (about the origin) from the 6 x 6 system; a user wind force (Fx, Fy) at (x, y) with Mz loads the level with Fx, Fy and Mz - Fx y + Fy x. Base shears sum k u per column; self-weight: material weight x A x height.",
